name payerne-radar-acm-1
timeout 300                                  # sim-seconds until TIMEOUT

# THE CROSSING TARGET: the reference geometry for systems/FBRadarSystem + modules/f16/FBF16Fcr. Two
# jets on perpendicular, level, constant-speed legs at the same altitude, so the true relative geometry
# is a straight line the analysis can recompute from the two telemetry files alone.
#
#   viper  flies due EAST from 46.700/6.800 -- the sensor; nose held on 090 by a single far waypoint
#   bandit flies due NORTH from 46.630/6.950 -- the target; radar OFF, so it contributes nothing but a
#          radar cross-section and, in the IFF mission next door, a transponder
#
# The bandit therefore starts 7.5 nm out at +34 deg off the viper's nose -- INSIDE the 10 nm ACM range
# gate but OUTSIDE every ACM azimuth box -- sweeps through the nose as the two legs converge, and
# finally passes down the left side. Three regimes in one run, in this order:
#
#   1. no contact at all         (az outside the sub-mode's box; the range gate never bites)
#   2. build-up -> firm track -> ACM auto-lock -> STT   (kHitsToFirm looks after the box is entered)
#   3. the target manoeuvres out of the antenna's reach -> coast -> RADAR_DROP / RADAR_LOST
#
# Regime 3 happens at the STT GIMBAL limit (+/-60 deg), not at the ACM box edge, because a lock takes
# the antenna out of its little search box and onto the target -- which is exactly what a lock IS
# (doc/modules/f16/radar-sensors.md). payerne-radar-bore.fbm is this same file with one word changed
# (acm_hud -> acm_bore): same geometry, a much narrower box, a measurably later acquisition.

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.70000 6.80000 3000 90.0 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                       # the 30x20 HUD-scan box, auto-locking
  wp 46.70000 7.20000 3000 300               # one far waypoint = a straight 090 leg

unit bandit
  module f16
  team hostile
  spawn 46.63000 6.95000 3000 0.0 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off                           # a pure target: it is looked at, it does not look
  set iff_xpdr off                           # no Mode-4 reply to give -- the contact stays UNKNOWN
  wp 46.85000 6.95000 3000 300               # one far waypoint = a straight 360 leg
